        "original_id": "5413aba7-800f-5167-8219-d1198f08715b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Die Macher, ZÈRTZ\n- People: Karl-Heinz Schmiel\n- Projects: GIPF Project\n- Concepts: German electoral system, political parties\n\nFacts:\n- Die Macher is a strategy board game designed by Karl-Heinz Schmiel of Germany.\n- Die Macher is based on the German electoral system.\n- In the 2006 edition of Die Macher, each player takes the role of one of five political parties: CDU/CSU, FDP, SPD, Greens, and Die Linke.\n- ZÈRTZ is the third game in the GIPF Project of six abstract strategy games.",
